VALUES ('ARX','published','Data-driven specialty-insurance marketplace connecting member underwriters with risk capital and reinsurance capacity.','Accelerant operates a risk exchange for specialty insurance, using data, technology and aligned capital structures to support member underwriting firms. Premium growth matters only with sound loss selection, reserve adequacy, reinsurance reliability and aligned related-party economics.','Marketplace, technology, data, portfolio management and capacity services for specialty-insurance underwriting members and capital providers.','Economics arise from risk-exchange and program fees, underwriting participation, investment results and related insurance or reinsurance arrangements.','Fragmented specialty underwriting can benefit from shared data, scalable capacity, faster workflows and diversified access to institutional risk capital.','Members must underwrite profitably, data must improve risk selection, reserves must remain adequate, capital partners must renew and conflicts across affiliates must be controlled.','Separate marketplace growth from retained insurance risk. Track gross and net premiums, loss ratio, fee take rate, reserves, ceded terms, capital-provider concentration and related-party transactions.','A networked risk exchange can scale specialty underwriting','["Member firms contribute specialized distribution and underwriting knowledge.","Shared data and technology can improve speed and portfolio visibility.","External capital can expand capacity without retaining every dollar of risk."]','Insurance losses and conflicts can overwhelm platform claims','["Reserve estimates may understate ultimate losses.","Reinsurance or capital providers can change terms or withdraw.","Related-party structures and concentrated members can misalign economics."]','The thesis breaks if premium and member growth fail to produce durable fee and underwriting returns after reserve development, reinsurance cost and capital dilution','[{"label":"PREMIUM / MEMBERS","value":"Marketplace scale","detail":"Gross written premium, member count, retention, mix and concentration"},{"label":"LOSS / RESERVES","value":"Risk quality","detail":"Current accident-year loss ratio, prior-year development, reserves and catastrophes"},{"label":"CAPITAL ECONOMICS","value":"Owner share","detail":"Ceded terms, fee take rate, investment result, related parties and tangible capital"}]','[{"title":"Underwriting and reserves","level":"High","text":"Specialty losses can emerge years after premium is written.","signal":"Loss ratio, reserve additions and prior-year development"},{"title":"Capacity and reinsurance","level":"High","text":"External capital may reprice or withdraw after losses.","signal":"Renewals, ceded cost, collateral and provider concentration"},{"title":"Governance and concentration","level":"High","text":"Affiliates and large members can create conflicts or dependency.","signal":"Related-party disclosures, member share and transaction terms"}]','[{"title":"Risk-adjusted growth","text":"Require premium and member expansion to preserve loss performance and reserve conservatism.","impact":"BULL CASE"},{"title":"Economic ownership","text":"Trace fees, retained risk, reinsurance and affiliate payments to the value remaining for common owners.","impact":"NEUTRAL"}]','["How much insurance risk ultimately remains on the balance sheet?","What reserve development would erase the reported underwriting advantage?","Are member and capital-provider contracts truly diversified and arm length?"]','Ryan Specialty, Kinsale Capital, Palomar, specialty MGAs, fronting carriers and insurance-capital marketplaces.','2026-03-18','2026-08-05T01:07:00Z',CURRENT_TIMESTAMP,CURRENT_TIMESTAMP)
