VALUES ('ASAN','published','Cloud work-management software company helping teams coordinate projects, goals, workflows and human-agent work.','Asana sells a collaborative work-management platform to individuals, teams and enterprises. Durable value depends on paid customer growth, enterprise expansion, retention, AI usefulness, gross margin and progress from losses to cash generation.','Cloud software for projects, tasks, goals, portfolios, workflows, reporting, administration, integrations and AI-assisted work coordination.','Subscription software sold in free and paid tiers, generally based on users and plan level, with enterprise contracts and usage-related AI features.','Organizations can consolidate fragmented collaboration tools and use AI agents within governed workflows, increasing seats and product depth.','Asana must prove measurable productivity, win enterprise deployments, retain users, control infrastructure and sales costs and offset stock-based compensation with durable cash generation.','Bookings and non-GAAP metrics need reconciliation to revenue, remaining performance obligations, dollar retention, free cash flow, stock compensation and diluted share growth.','A shared work graph can coordinate people and AI agents','["Workflows and integrations become more useful as teams standardize on one platform.","Enterprise governance can expand seat and product adoption.","AI-assisted execution can deepen usage if it saves measurable time."]','Crowded collaboration markets and dilution constrain value','["Microsoft, Atlassian, Monday.com and many point tools compete aggressively.","Seat growth and retention may weaken as customers optimize software spend.","Persistent stock compensation and losses can dilute owners despite revenue growth."]','The thesis breaks if enterprise and AI adoption fail to sustain retention and cash generation after stock compensation and sales investment','[{"label":"CUSTOMERS / RETENTION","value":"Demand durability","detail":"Paid customers, large accounts, seat expansion, churn and dollar-based retention"},{"label":"REVENUE / RPO","value":"Growth visibility","detail":"Subscription revenue, billings, remaining obligations, enterprise and AI mix"},{"label":"CASH / DILUTION","value":"Owner conversion","detail":"Free cash flow, stock compensation, share count and operating margin"}]','[{"title":"Competition","level":"High","text":"Bundled suites and focused tools can limit pricing and adoption.","signal":"Win rates, pricing, churn and enterprise growth"},{"title":"AI monetization","level":"Medium","text":"AI features may add cost without durable willingness to pay.","signal":"Usage, paid conversion, compute cost and customer outcomes"},{"title":"Dilution and execution","level":"High","text":"Stock compensation and sales spending can outpace owner cash returns.","signal":"Share count, SBC, free cash flow and GAAP margin"}]','[{"title":"Enterprise expansion","text":"Track large-customer growth and retention with evidence of company-wide workflow standardization.","impact":"BULL CASE"},{"title":"Per-share economics","text":"Require revenue and free cash flow to grow faster than diluted shares and stock compensation.","impact":"NEUTRAL"}]','["Does AI usage produce incremental revenue after compute cost?","Which enterprise cohorts are expanding seats and products?","When does GAAP per-share profitability become self-sustaining?"]','Microsoft, Atlassian, Monday.com, Smartsheet, Notion, ClickUp and other collaboration and project-management platforms.','2026-03-13','2026-08-05T01:07:00Z',CURRENT_TIMESTAMP,CURRENT_TIMESTAMP)
