VALUES ('ASB','published','Midwest regional bank holding company providing commercial, consumer and wealth-management services.','Associated Banc-Corp gathers deposits and lends across Wisconsin and other Midwest markets. Deposit cost, net interest margin, commercial credit, fee income, capital and acquisition integration determine per-share value.','Deposit accounts, commercial and industrial loans, commercial real-estate loans, residential mortgages, consumer lending, treasury services, wealth and private banking.','Net interest income from loans and securities funded by deposits and borrowings, plus wealth, card, service and other fee income.','Relationship deposits, commercial-market share, fee services and disciplined expansion can grow earnings and tangible book value.','Associated must retain deposits, price loans for risk, manage commercial concentrations, integrate growth, control expenses and preserve liquidity and regulatory capital.','For a bank, track deposit mix and beta, securities marks, criticized loans, office and CRE exposure, allowance coverage, tangible common equity and per-share book value.','A scaled Midwest relationship franchise can compound','["Commercial relationships can support deposits, lending and fee cross-selling.","A diversified Midwest footprint can reduce single-market dependence.","Operating scale and disciplined expansion can improve efficiency."]','Funding, credit and integration errors can impair capital','["Deposit competition can compress margin and liquidity.","Commercial real-estate and business credit can deteriorate in a downturn.","Acquisition and restructuring costs can dilute tangible book value."]','The thesis breaks if deposit repricing, credit losses or expansion costs cause sustained deterioration in tangible capital and book value per share','[{"label":"DEPOSITS / NIM","value":"Core earnings","detail":"Deposit balance and mix, funding cost, asset yield and net interest margin"},{"label":"CREDIT QUALITY","value":"Downside control","detail":"Criticized assets, nonperformers, charge-offs, allowance and concentrations"},{"label":"CAPITAL / EFFICIENCY","value":"Owner outcome","detail":"Tangible equity, regulatory ratios, expenses, dividends and diluted shares"}]','[{"title":"Funding and rates","level":"High","text":"Deposit repricing and asset duration can pressure margin and liquidity.","signal":"Deposit beta, uninsured deposits, borrowings and NIM"},{"title":"Commercial credit","level":"High","text":"CRE and business loans can produce concentrated losses.","signal":"Criticized loans, office exposure, nonperformers and charge-offs"},{"title":"Integration and regulation","level":"Medium","text":"Growth projects and compliance demands can raise cost or capital needs.","signal":"Merger milestones, expenses, capital ratios and regulatory actions"}]','[{"title":"Deposit franchise","text":"Track relationship balances, mix and pricing instead of headline deposit growth alone.","impact":"BULL CASE"},{"title":"Per-share capital","text":"Require earnings and strategic expansion to increase tangible book value after credit costs.","impact":"NEUTRAL"}]','["How much margin recovery depends on lower deposit rates?","Which commercial loan pools have the greatest loss sensitivity?","Will expansion increase tangible book value per share after all costs?"]','Huntington Bancshares, U.S. Bancorp, BMO, Old National, Wintrust and other Midwest regional and community banks.','2026-02-12','2026-08-05T01:07:00Z',CURRENT_TIMESTAMP,CURRENT_TIMESTAMP)
