VALUES ('ASC','published','Owner and operator of product and chemical tankers serving global seaborne trades.','Ardmore Shipping earns voyage and time-charter revenue by transporting refined petroleum products and chemicals. Spot rates, utilization, fleet quality, operating cost, fuel efficiency and capital allocation dominate results.','Marine transportation using a fleet of medium-range product and chemical tankers.','Voyage-charter and time-charter revenue, net of voyage expenses, with earnings tied to daily rates, fleet days and utilization.','A constrained tanker orderbook, longer trade routes and efficient vessels can support rates and cash generation during favorable cycles.','Ardmore must operate safely, maintain vessels, secure profitable employment, manage fuel and emissions rules and allocate cyclical cash without overpaying for ships.','Annualize neither peak nor trough rates. Track time-charter equivalent revenue, operating days, off-hire, vessel age, drydocking, debt, newbuilding prices and net asset value.','A disciplined modern fleet can harvest tight tanker markets','["Product and chemical trades require specialized global transport.","Efficient vessels can earn better economics and meet tightening rules.","Strong cycle cash flow can reduce debt or fund accretive fleet renewal."]','Shipping cycles can reverse faster than capital plans','["Spot rates are volatile and sensitive to trade flows and fleet supply.","Vessel values and residual assumptions can fall with rates.","Accidents, off-hire, regulation and poorly timed acquisitions can destroy cash."]','The thesis breaks if normalized vessel earnings fail to cover operating, drydock and capital costs while fleet value and per-share net asset value decline','[{"label":"TCE RATE / DAYS","value":"Revenue engine","detail":"Spot and time-charter rates, operating days, utilization and off-hire"},{"label":"FLEET COST / VALUE","value":"Asset economics","detail":"Opex, drydock, fuel efficiency, vessel age and market values"},{"label":"CAPITAL ALLOCATION","value":"Owner outcome","detail":"Debt, dividends, buybacks, acquisitions and net asset value per share"}]','[{"title":"Freight cycle","level":"High","text":"Rates can fall sharply when trade or vessel supply changes.","signal":"Spot indices, fixtures, orderbook, scrapping and tonne-miles"},{"title":"Asset and operating","level":"High","text":"Vessel values, downtime and repair costs can impair returns.","signal":"Off-hire, drydock, opex, impairments and fleet age"},{"title":"Regulation and safety","level":"Medium","text":"Emissions rules and incidents can require capital or interrupt trading.","signal":"Compliance capex, fuel use, spills, detentions and insurance"}]','[{"title":"Through-cycle earnings","text":"Compare realized TCE with full operating, drydock and replacement capital costs.","impact":"NEUTRAL"},{"title":"Per-share NAV discipline","text":"Judge ship purchases, sales and distributions by their effect on net asset value per share.","impact":"BULL CASE"}]','["What daily rate covers full-cycle vessel and replacement cost?","How much fleet value is exposed to older or less efficient ships?","Will peak-cycle cash be returned, delevered or reinvested at attractive prices?"]','Scorpio Tankers, TORM, Hafnia, International Seaways and other product and chemical tanker owners.','2026-03-06','2026-08-05T01:07:00Z',CURRENT_TIMESTAMP,CURRENT_TIMESTAMP)
