VALUES ('ASIX','published','Vertically integrated U.S. producer of nylon solutions, chemical intermediates and plant nutrients.','AdvanSix converts ammonia and other inputs through an integrated manufacturing chain into caprolactam, nylon resin, ammonium sulfate fertilizer, acetone and related chemicals. Commodity spreads, plant reliability, mix and capital intensity drive returns.','Nylon 6 resin and intermediates, caprolactam, ammonium sulfate plant nutrients, acetone, phenol-chain co-products and related chemicals.','Product sales priced through contracts and market formulas, with earnings shaped by raw-material cost, commodity benchmarks, product mix and plant utilization.','Integrated plants, domestic supply, differentiated nylon applications and higher-value plant-nutrient or chemical products can improve through-cycle economics.','Facilities must operate safely and reliably, price must cover natural-gas and ammonia inputs, environmental obligations must be funded and capital projects must earn adequate returns.','Reported sales can move with commodity prices. Track market spreads, utilization, planned and unplanned outages, fertilizer seasonality, working capital, environmental reserves and sustaining capital.','Integration can capture value across essential chemistries','["A connected production chain creates co-product and operating efficiencies.","Domestic assets can benefit customers seeking reliable regional supply.","Specialty nylon and plant-nutrient mix can improve commodity economics."]','Commodity spreads and plant concentration create volatility','["Natural-gas, ammonia and benchmark-price moves can compress spreads.","Major plant outages can reduce multiple products simultaneously.","Environmental, safety and sustaining-capital obligations can absorb cash."]','The thesis breaks if normalized spreads and plant reliability cannot cover sustaining, environmental and growth capital while producing adequate free cash flow','[{"label":"MARKET SPREADS","value":"Cycle economics","detail":"Nylon, caprolactam, fertilizer and co-product pricing versus natural gas and ammonia"},{"label":"UTILIZATION / OUTAGES","value":"Operating leverage","detail":"Throughput, turnarounds, unplanned downtime, yield and fixed-cost absorption"},{"label":"CAPITAL / CASH","value":"Owner outcome","detail":"Maintenance, environmental and growth capital, working capital and free cash flow"}]','[{"title":"Commodity and input price","level":"High","text":"Product prices may fall or lag natural-gas and ammonia costs.","signal":"Benchmark spreads, pass-through timing and inventories"},{"title":"Plant operations","level":"High","text":"Integrated-site outages can affect several product chains.","signal":"Utilization, turnaround scope, incidents and repair cost"},{"title":"Environmental and capital","level":"High","text":"Legacy and ongoing compliance obligations require cash.","signal":"Reserves, remediation, emissions projects and sustaining capex"}]','[{"title":"Normalized spread and uptime","text":"Measure earnings across commodity seasons and include planned and unplanned outage economics.","impact":"NEUTRAL"},{"title":"Capital productivity","text":"Require specialty and expansion projects to improve free cash flow after full maintenance and environmental spending.","impact":"BULL CASE"}]','["What normalized spread supports acceptable returns through a cycle?","How much cash is required for reliable and compliant operations?","Which mix initiatives are truly differentiated from commodity pricing?"]','BASF, Ascend Performance Materials, Highsun, UBE, domestic fertilizer producers and global nylon and chemical suppliers.','2026-02-20','2026-08-05T01:07:00Z',CURRENT_TIMESTAMP,CURRENT_TIMESTAMP)
